          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20984 obdclass: wake OJS_CLEANING waiters in jobstats",
        "message": "LU-20984 obdclass: wake OJS_CLEANING waiters in jobstats\n\n\"lctl set_param *.job_stats=clear\" or umount that arrives while a\nperiodic jobstats cleanup is running hangs forever in D state in\nlprocfs_job_cleanup().\n\nThe forced cleanup waits for OJS_CLEANING with wait_on_bit(), but the\nholder drops the bit with a plain clear_bit() and nothing ever calls\nwake_up_bit(), so the waiter is never woken.  job_reclaim_rcu() has\nthe same problem for OJS_ACTIVE_JOBS, costing a 30s stall at fini.\n\nUse clear_and_wake_up_bit() for both bits.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: cad59b9b72fc (\"LU-18351 obdclass: jobstat scaling\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8d937a7481f2c40fa00bba850ebf80eb3e2a6577\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
